## Summary

Shipped a production-grade native Apple `TimelineScrubber` shared surface (P4/0107) at full parity with `components/data-display/TimelineScrubber.tsx`, following the established `feature-views/AiUsageCard` 9-file convention.

**Delivered** (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/`, 11 files, 2114 lines):
- Interactive scrubber reproducing the web body: track + buffered + neon fill, all **8 marker kinds** (focusable buttons + `.help` tooltips + cluster badges), hover ghost playhead, drag thumb (grows + rings while scrubbing), hover/drag **preview tooltip** (time + speed/power/soc/elevation), optional decorative background.
- Interactions: tap-seek, drag-scrub with **50 ms throttled intermediate seeks**, marker-tap-seek, pointer hover preview — all via a P1/S8 state-holder seam (no HTTP in the view).
- Every P4 leaf state renders: **loading / empty / error / data**, plus the orthogonal **live/stale/offline** axis (chip + banner + one-shot stale auto-refresh).
- Accessibility: track is one adjustable slider (label + m:ss value + increment/decrement); each marker a labeled button. Reduce-motion honored; `view.opened` telemetry; 22/22 i18n keys catalogued.

**Verification (all green, real evidence in the log):**
- `xcodebuild build test` on **iOS Simulator (iPhone 16)** → BUILD + TEST SUCCEEDED, **37/37**
- `xcodebuild build-for-testing` on **macOS** + direct `xcrun xctest` → **37/37**
- SwiftPM (Swift 6, complete concurrency) → 37/37; `swiftlint --strict` → **0 violations**; `swiftformat --lint` → **0/10**; placeholder gate → **0**

Compiled against the **real** design tokens + shared components. The full app-scheme `xcodebuild` was unrunnable in-scope (shared-surfaces not yet in `project.yml`; `Shared.xcframework` unstaged — both outside the allowed files), so I verified via a temporary scoped Xcode project — documented honestly in the gate log (`EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE`). Pre-existing unrelated working-tree changes were left untouched.

